# /services/pwrmgr — power manager (platform shutdown / reboot).
#
# svcmgr launches pwrmgr post-handover as a provider. `provides` makes
# svcmgr create pwrmgr's service endpoint, serve its RECV as bootstrap
# cap[0], and publish two SENDs on it:
#   * pwrmgr.shutdown:auth — SHUTDOWN_AUTHORITY-tokened (1 << 63), for
#     consumers permitted to power the platform off; seed-only, so only
#     recipes that seed it hold it.
#   * pwrmgr.deny:deny    — a no-authority twin (sentinel token 1) that the
#     SHUTDOWN/REBOOT gate rejects; svctest uses it to assert the deny path.
# `seed = devmgr.shutdown acpid.power` delivers cap[1] and cap[2]:
#   * devmgr.shutdown — the REGISTRY_QUERY_AUTHORITY |
#     SHUTDOWN_DEVICE_AUTHORITY-tokened SEND on devmgr's registry; on
#     RISC-V pwrmgr acquires its SbiControl through QUERY_SHUTDOWN_DEVICE.
#     pwrmgr is the only recipe seeding it.
#   * acpid.power — the POWER_AUTHORITY-tokened SEND on acpid's endpoint; on
#     x86-64 pwrmgr powers off and resets through acpid's SLEEP(5) and RESET,
#     and waits in its WAIT_EVENT for the power button
#     (services/acpid/README.md § Power requests). svcmgr launches acpid
#     before pwrmgr because of this seed.
# Each architecture deletes the seed it does not use. devmgr is the hardware
# authority and acpid holds the ACPI registers; on x86-64 pwrmgr also holds a
# derivation from acpid's QUERY_SLEEP of its capability over PM1a_CNT, or
# over SLEEP_CONTROL_REG on a hardware-reduced platform, for its core-death
# power-off.
#
# `restart = on_failure`: svcmgr re-creates pwrmgr from /services/pwrmgr and
# re-serves a fresh RECV on the persistent endpoint, so a SHUTDOWN_AUTHORITY
# cap cached against `pwrmgr.shutdown` survives a crash-restart. pwrmgr
# re-acquires its RISC-V SbiControl from devmgr on each (re)start.
# `shutdown_actuator = pwrmgr.shutdown` declares pwrmgr the system's
# shutdown actuator: when a `critical = yes` service is permanently down,
# svcmgr calls SHUTDOWN through a SEND it derives from pwrmgr's endpoint
# with the `pwrmgr.shutdown` entry's SHUTDOWN_AUTHORITY badge, and serves
# pwrmgr as cap[3] the RECV-only derivation of the core-death queue, on
# which pwrmgr observes the death of svcmgr, memmgr and procmgr and powers
# the platform off. svcmgr creates pwrmgr pinned (CREATE_PINNED) for this role.
# `critical = no`: a permanently-dead pwrmgr cannot power the system off,
# so a graceful shutdown on its death is impossible; the honest terminal
# state is logged-and-continue, matching timed.
binary            = /services/pwrmgr
priority          = 16
restart           = on_failure
critical          = no
namespace         = none
provides          = pwrmgr.shutdown:auth pwrmgr.deny:deny
seed              = devmgr.shutdown acpid.power
shutdown_actuator = pwrmgr.shutdown
